WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.000
The trucks roll out at six.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:04.760
Back in the shop,

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.280
a binder says who's trained and who isn't.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.320
A spreadsheet tracks renewals.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.460
Incident reports live on paper.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.260
And when an inspector asks

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.180
for proof, the hunt begins.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.400
This is IntelliSafe.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.220
Annual safety training, incident reporting,

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.940
and site inspections built

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.240
for public works crews.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:25.520
One place, one record.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.200
Training starts with 19 modules,

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.000
one for each of OSHA's

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.560
10 most cited standards,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.840
plus pole top and bucket truck rescue,

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.820
confined spaces, electrical safety, and more.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.460
Every module is written for public works

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.080
with examples from the field,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.420
not a factory floor.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.000
Each one ends with a 10 question quiz.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.060
80% passes, every attempt is recorded,

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.100
and a certificate prints on completion.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.640
Pass a module, and next year's assignment

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.480
is created automatically, due 12 months out.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.640
Nobody has to chase people down.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.260
Employees get a reminder

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.180
30 days before training is due,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.140
again at seven, and every week it's overdue.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:05.920
Supervisors get a copy.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.820
When something happens, the report is ready.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:10.340
Eight sections,

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.820
the same ones on your paper form.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.220
Circle the damage on the vehicle diagram.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.600
Mark the injury on the body diagram.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.340
Sketch the scene.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.700
Witness statements are signed

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.760
on screen or through an emailed link.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.460
The report won't close until the root cause

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.360
and corrective actions are on record.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:27.720
Then it prints,

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.700
diagrams and signatures included.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:30.880
Site inspections

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.600
and the annual program audit are

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.480
built in, every item tied

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:35.640
to its OSHA reference.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.280
The safety manager sees

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.500
every employee against every course.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.400
On track, overdue, by division.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.600
Excel export in one click.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:46.260
Crews can open it today

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.860
on any phone or computer.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.460
Nothing to install.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:50.760
When you want accounts,

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.160
assignments by division,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.180
and automatic email,

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.000
the full platform runs on your own server.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:57.680
Every crew trained.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.420
Every incident on record.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.240
Proof when you need it.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.620
IntelliSafe.
